# About This Project
#
# This project is an ongoing Litex formalization inspired by Terence Tao's
# Analysis II. It follows the book's development from metric spaces and
# continuity through Fourier analysis, multivariable calculus, measure, and
# integration. It is an independent translation project, not an official
# edition of or substitute for the original book.
#
# Most declarations included here are accepted by the Litex verifier, but the
# project is not a complete formalization of every argument in the source. All
# known unchecked steps remain visible as explicit trust boundaries. Some
# reflect proof steps that the original exposition leaves to exercises or
# compresses; others expose current gaps in Litex's library, automation, or the
# translation itself. We fill in implicit reasoning where it illuminates the
# mathematics, while occasionally retaining a clearly marked omission to
# preserve the source's pace and avoid obscuring the main ideas with routine
# infrastructure.
#
# The chapters on metric-space convergence, uniform convergence, power and
# Fourier series, several-variable calculus, Lebesgue measure, and Lebesgue
# integration provide particularly interesting examples of Litex handling
# layered definitions and long dependency chains. They also make the remaining
# boundaries of the system concrete rather than hiding them.
#
# We hope readers learn useful analysis from the formal development and see how
# Litex turns mathematical statements into readable, reusable, and checkable
# facts while reporting unfinished proof obligations honestly.
